# /etc/auros/kiosk.conf -- the one application a kiosk machine runs.
#
# apply-policy REFUSES to build a kiosk image unless this file exists with a KIOSK_EXEC, or
# AUROS_KIOSK_EXEC is passed to it. A kiosk image that boots to a black screen because nobody named
# an application is not a degraded product, it is a brick, and it would pass every check that only
# looks at what was removed.
#
# A recipe supplies this file, or passes AUROS_KIOSK_EXEC=... to apply-policy and lets it write one.
#
# The value is a shell command line, run as the unprivileged `auroskiosk` account inside the
# compositor. Examples:
#
#   KIOSK_EXEC="flatpak run --branch=stable org.mozilla.firefox --kiosk https://library.example.org"
#   KIOSK_EXEC="flatpak run org.chromium.Chromium --kiosk --incognito https://catalogue.example.org"
#   KIOSK_EXEC="/usr/bin/my-signage-player /etc/auros/playlist.json"
#
# This file is .example on purpose: it is documentation, not configuration. The real file has no
# suffix and is written by the recipe or by apply-policy.
KIOSK_EXEC=""
